Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: an unused color target is absent, not rgba8unorm

An unused fragment output location was being turned into a real render target.

  WGPUTextureFormat fmt = WGPUTextureFormat_RGBA8Unorm; // Placeholder for unused slots.
  ...
  color_targets[i].format = fmt;
  if (p_color_attachments[i] == ATTACHMENT_UNUSED) {
      color_targets[i].writeMask = WGPUColorWriteMask_None;

Masking the writes does not make a target absent. It stays a real rgba8unorm
target for render-pass compatibility, while the render-pass path in this same
driver already emits a null view for the identical slot. The two sides therefore
disagreed on every Forward+ scene pipeline:

  pipeline  [rgba16float, rgba8unorm, rgba8unorm] + depth32float-stencil8
  pass      [rgba16float, null,       null      ] + depth32float-stencil8

  Attachment state of [RenderPipeline "SceneForwardClusteredShaderRD:19"] is not
  compatible with [RenderPassEncoder]

An unused location now emits WGPUTextureFormat_Undefined, which is how a null
entry in the JS fragment.targets sequence is expressed through the C API. Holes
are preserved in place rather than compacted: Godot reserves stable @location()s
for optional outputs such as separate specular and motion vectors, so
[used, unused, used] has to keep its middle hole.

Measured on a Tesla P40 through Chrome/WebGPU, Chariot on Forward+:

  attachment-state incompatibility   1018 -> 0
  cascading invalid CommandBuffer    1005 -> 0
  GPUValidationError                 9004 -> 4780

Confirmed by pairing rather than by count: tests/browser/pass-trace.mjs records
every setPipeline against the pass it was issued inside, and reports 44 distinct
pipeline/pass pairs with ZERO mismatches. Comparing independent lists of
pipelines and passes is what produced a wrong diagnosis earlier in this
investigation -- the [rgba8unorm], no-depth passes turned out to be Tonemap and
Canvas, not the scene pass.

Still no frame. Remaining distinct classes are unrelated to attachments:
sampler2DMS binding, comparison-sampler-as-non-comparison, and two storage
format-promotion mismatches (R8Unorm vs RGBA8Unorm, R16Float view of R32Float).

diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
--- a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
@@ -8473,8 +8473,31 @@
 	memset(blend_states.ptr(), 0, sizeof(WGPUBlendState) * color_target_count);
 
 	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < color_target_count; i++) {
+		// A fragment output location Godot marks unused must become an ABSENT entry
+		// in fragment.targets, not a real target with its writes masked off.
+		// WGPUTextureFormat_Undefined is how a null entry in the JS targets sequence
+		// is expressed through the C API.
+		//
+		// A placeholder RGBA8Unorm here stays a real target for render-pass
+		// compatibility purposes, and the render-pass path already emits a null view
+		// for the very same slot -- so the two sides of this driver disagreed, and
+		// every Forward+ scene pipeline was rejected:
+		//
+		//   pipeline  [rgba16float, rgba8unorm, rgba8unorm] + depth32float-stencil8
+		//   pass      [rgba16float, null,       null      ] + depth32float-stencil8
+		//
+		// Godot reserves stable @location()s for optional outputs (separate specular,
+		// motion vectors). When those are inactive the location is a hole, so holes
+		// are preserved in place rather than compacted away -- [used, unused, used]
+		// has to keep its middle hole.
+		if (p_color_attachments[i] == ATTACHMENT_UNUSED) {
+			color_targets[i].format = WGPUTextureFormat_Undefined;
+			color_targets[i].writeMask = WGPUColorWriteMask_None;
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		// Get texture format from subpass color reference i.
-		WGPUTextureFormat fmt = WGPUTextureFormat_RGBA8Unorm; // Placeholder for unused slots.
+		WGPUTextureFormat fmt = WGPUTextureFormat_RGBA8Unorm; // Fallback if the reference is missing.
 		if (i < (uint32_t)subpass.color_references.size()) {
 			int32_t att_idx = subpass.color_references[i].attachment;
 			if (att_idx != ATTACHMENT_UNUSED && (uint32_t)att_idx < (uint32_t)rp->attachments.size()) {
@@ -8495,11 +8518,6 @@
 		}
 		color_targets[i].format = fmt;
 
-		if (p_color_attachments[i] == ATTACHMENT_UNUSED) {
-			color_targets[i].writeMask = WGPUColorWriteMask_None;
-			continue;
-		}
-
 		// Blend state from p_blend_state.attachments[i].
 		if (i < (uint32_t)p_blend_state.attachments.size()) {
 			const PipelineColorBlendState::Attachment &ba = p_blend_state.attachments[i];
